  "honest_findings_verdict": "Clearly reported null result: Under severe sensor faults and extreme OOD severities, lambda_phys = 0.1 yields a marginal, non-significant gain in onset accuracy (+1.07%, p=0.3438) while increasing margin estimation error (3.10s vs 2.27s, p=0.0098, d=1.24). lambda_phys = 1.0 further degrades margin error to 7.12s. The capacity-matched non-physics regularizer achieves equivalent onset accuracy (75.73%, p=1.0000) and lower margin MAE (2.24s) without distortion. Physics loss regularizers do not provide a statistically significant advantage over capacity-matched non-physics regularizers under severe sensor faults."
